Task: Your mission is to complete the `Spaceship` class to properly manage its fuel level using encapsulation. The fuel level should be a private field, accessible and modifiable only through designated methods. Implement the `takeOff`, `refuel`, and `getFuelLevel` methods to ensure safe fuel operations.

Submitted code:
```
class Spaceship {
  // 1. Declare the private field
  #fuel;
  static MAX_FUEL = 100;
  static TAKEOFF_COST = 10;

  constructor(initialFuel) {
    // Ensure initial fuel is within the 0-100 range
    this.#fuel = Math.min(Spaceship.MAX_FUEL, Math.max(0, initialFuel));
  }

  takeOff() {
    // Check if we have enough fuel for the maneuver
    if (this.#fuel >= Spaceship.TAKEOFF_COST) {
      this.#fuel -= Spaceship.TAKEOFF_COST;
      return true;
    }

    console.log("Not enough fuel for takeoff!");
    return false;
  }

  refuel(amount) {
    // Add fuel but cap it at the maximum capacity
    this.#fuel = Math.min(Spaceship.MAX_FUEL, this.#fuel + amount);
  }

  getFuelLevel() {
    // Provide read-only access to the private state
    return this.#fuel;
  }
}

// --- Example Usage ---
const shuttle = new Spaceship(50);
console.log(shuttle.getFuelLevel()); // 50

if (shuttle.takeOff()) {
  console.log("Takeoff successful!");
}

console.log(shuttle.getFuelLevel()); // 40

shuttle.refuel(70);
console.log(shuttle.getFuelLevel()); // 100 (capped at MAX_FUEL)
```

